Modifications: the files were modified. SKILL.md was written fresh in the
house style as the single Godot entry point, with a routing table to the other
godot-* and game-* plugins and a hand-off to the godot-mcp editor addon's own
skill. The upstream skills were merged and condensed into 21 references,
GDScript only (C# moved to godot-csharp). Facts were rechecked against the
Godot 4.7 documentation (class reference, TSCN format page, import docs and
the 4.3 to 4.7 migration guides). version-notes.md and tscn-tres-format.md are
new; the latter updates Qb-Lab's rules for 4.6 (load_steps no longer written,
per-node unique_id, uid attributes on ext_resource lines, .uid sidecar files
since 4.4). Fixes on port: print_debug prints in every build; CanvasGroup does
not batch and OS.gc() does not exist; texture filter and repeat are CanvasItem
or material settings, not import flags, the compress default is Lossless and
the occluder suffixes are -occ/-occonly; a Camera2D roll needs
ignore_rotation = false and follow smoothing uses 1 - exp(-k*delta);
is_action_just_pressed is tick-aware in _physics_process; NavigationAgent2D
path_desired_distance defaults to 20; collision shapes stay direct children of
their body; there is no make_unique() method; EditorPlugin docks use
add_dock(EditorDock); @tool scripts ship in exports and C# #if TOOLS wraps only
editor-only classes; a nested state machine no longer starts itself; saves use
an atomic temp-file rename with a backup, and user-writable .tres files are
never loaded; registries use ResourceLoader.list_directory instead of
DirAccess scans; push_error replaces assert in code headless runs reach.
